	FV2021 Coleopteran (40 MP)
		A three-metre talk British-built humanoid combat walker used by the Canadians on Mars.  They use a new “mind-interface” neuro-helmet that makes the mecha very agile.  However, if a different pilot wants to use the mecha, the neuro-helmet must be “retuned” to their brain waves — this takes a full day; until then, halve the Defence Mastery and Combat Technique: Lightning Reflexes Attribute bonuses.  The mecha are painted standard colours: UN white, with sky-blue helmets. 
		**Derived Values**
			AR 20
			HP 80
		**Mecha Sub-Attributes** (43 MP)
			Accessories 2 (Radio, Inertial Navigation. 2 MP)
			Ground Speed 1 (Up to 50 kph. 2 MP)
			Heavy Armour 2 (Partial, thin. 7 MP)
			Life Support 2 (2 MP)
			Manoeuvre Bonus 4 (Ground only; +2 to Initiative and +2 to Defense Combat Value. 4 MP)
			Sensors 1 (Range to 10 kilometres (1,000 km in space). 1 MP)
			Super-Strength 1 (3 MP)
			Toughness 2 (+40 Health Points. 8 MP)
			Weapon: Plasma Fist 2 (Damage ACV+60, Melee, Limited Shots: 6 shots. 1 MP)
			Weapon: Railgun 3 (Damage ACV+45, Long-Range: 5 km, Unreliable. 12 MP)
			Weapon: Rocket Pod 2 (Damage ACV+45, Auto-fire, Area Effect, Limited Shots ×2: 3 shots, Stoppable. 1 MP)
		**Mecha Defects** (3 MBP)
			Awkward Size (Large: 1-10 tonnes. 2 MBP)
			Hanger Queen (1 MBP)
		**Notes**
			Punch: Damage ACV+10, Muscle-Powered, Melee
